  "notes": "Drawn from one right-side photo (N255CM, 767-300, October 2024); the left side is assumed to mirror it. Older aircraft still carry ATI's previous white scheme with the blue 'ATI' logo forward (N763CX, 2022). Most ATI 767s fly in Amazon Prime Air or DHL colors. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on N255CM (right side, 2024-10-03; its outline is a 767-200's, so drawnOn B762): AIR TRANSPORT runs x 0.177-0.427 with its cap top at y ~0.46 (it had been drawn ~30% too tall); INTERNATIONAL, half its height, sits under the forward end of TRANSPORT on the right side, right-aligned as read: no photo shows the left side, where it would likely sit under the aft end, so it is drawn on the right only.",
  "history": "Replaces Skyarium v1's approximate standard (a few colors from memory). ATI's earlier scheme was all white with a blue swept 'ATI' and globe logo ahead of the wing."
